* Chicken Directions

1. Mix large spoonfuls of black pepper, paprika, garlic powder, and corn starch
   together. Add more of whichever seasonings you prefer, to taste.

   #+ATTR_HTML: :width 400
   [[file:../recipes_img/seasoning.jpg]]

   The picture only illustrates the color, not the amount.

2. Cut the chicken into small chunks, preferably nickel-to-quarter sized.
3. Heat a large skillet to medium-high (6 on my electric stove).
4. Put a thin layer of the mixed seasoning on the bottom of the mixing bowl,
   then add the diced chicken.
5. Apply a hefty coating of seasoning onto the chicken, salt to taste, then mix
   until the chicken is well seasoned.
6. Add vegetable oil to the hot skillet and place the diced chicken in.
7. Set a timer for 8 minutes and let the chicken cook, flipping halfway
   through.

This takes adjusting to your stove. Have a meat thermometer on hand to make
sure the chicken reaches 165 °F, and try not to char it.

* Sauce Directions

1. Add 1 cup of soy sauce to a small sauce pan (watered down if you'd like).
2. Put the sauce pan over medium-low heat.
3. Add one spoonful of gochujang paste.
4. Add honey to taste.
5. Stir. If it's too spicy, add more honey; if it's too sweet, add more soy
   sauce or gochujang paste.

   The heat is only there to make the ingredients less viscous.

6. Add the sauce to the cooked chicken, reserving some in a separate container
   if you want.

* Serve

Cook 3/4–1 cup of rice on the stove and combine it with the chicken and sauce.

If you're feeling fancy, slice a zucchini in half and cut it into half-inch
slices. Put them on an oiled skillet, salt and pepper them, and cook on both
sides. Add to the bowl for vegetables.
